; DOMAIN: tamagawa-number [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: The Bloch-Kato Tamagawa number conjecture (Fontaine-Perrin-Riou formulation) refines Beilinson's rational-covolume statement into an exact equality. For a motive M over Q with p-adic realization V, form the fundamental line Delta(M) = det_Q H^*_f(M) tensor det_Q^{-1} of the motivic/Betti-de Rham comparison. Fontaine-Perrin-Riou: the L-value L^*(M,0) trivializes Delta(M) integrally — the leading Taylor coefficient equals the covolume of a canonical Z_p-lattice det R Gamma_c(Z[1/S], T) under the period-regulator isomorphism, with NO undetermined rational: L^*(M,0) = (period x regulator x #Sha(M)) / (#H^0 x #H^2 torsion x prod Tamagawa_l). The equivariant version (ETNC, Burns-Flach) upgrades this to a statement in the relative K-group K_0(Z[G],R) over a Galois group G, unifying Beilinson, Bloch-Kato, Stark, and the Main Conjecture. This is the exact-equality apex refining beilinson_conjecture, with bloch_kato providing the local Tamagawa factors and perrin_riou providing the p-adic trivialization.
; Bridge: genesis_beilinson_conjecture (Tamagawa conjecture is the exact Tamagawa-number refinement of Beilinson's L^*(M,n) ~_Q covolume, fixing the rational ambiguity to (period x regulator x #Sha)/(torsion x Tamagawa factors) via the fundamental line) + genesis_bloch_kato (the local Bloch-Kato Selmer conditions H^1_f define the finite parts H^*_f(M) entering the fundamental line, and the local Tamagawa factors prod Tam_l are the Bloch-Kato local terms) + genesis_perrin_riou (Perrin-Riou's big exponential provides the p-adic trivialization of the fundamental line, matching the p-part of the Tamagawa equality to the Iwasawa Main Conjecture).
(= (fundamental-line $M) (tensor (det (h-f $M)) (det-inv (comparison $M))))
(= (trivialize $M) (equal (leading-l-value $M) (covolume (det (r-gamma-c $M)))))
(= (tamagawa-number-conjecture $M) (equal (leading-l-value $M) (over (times (period $M) (regulator $M) (sha $M)) (times (torsion $M) (local-tamagawa $M)))))
(= (equivariant-tnc $M $G) (statement (k0 (group-ring $G)) (fundamental-line $M)))
(= (refines (tamagawa-number-conjecture $M) (beilinson-conjecture $M)) (exact-equality))